  "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#semiotic_projection_1",
  "@type": "SemioticProjection",
  "instance_name": "semiotic_projection_1",
  "label": "User projected onto the rhetorical question and the visual interaction",
  "description": "The user is projected onto the rhetorical question posed in the text ('you're asking people for 5 cents a day?') and the visual scene of the woman questioning the child. The text directly addresses the woman as 'you', making the user identify with the speaker of the rhetorical question. The user is also projected onto the scene of the questioning interaction, as the visual material of the woman looking down at the child is used to represent the person being questioned, thereby inviting the user to imagine themselves in the role of the critic or the moral arbiter. The projection is onto both the textual material (the rhetorical question) and the visual material (the woman's expression and posture), creating a dual projection that frames the user as the one judging the situation.",
  "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface",
